#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:5
msgid "AD9910 driver"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:7
msgid ""
"Direct Digital Synthesizer (DDS) driver for the Analog Devices Inc. AD9910. "
"The module name is ``ad9910``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:10
msgid "`AD9910 <https://www.analog.com/en/products/ad9910.html>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:12
msgid ""
"The AD9910 is a 1 GSPS DDS with a 14-bit DAC, controlled over SPI. The "
"driver exposes the device through a hierarchy of typed IIO output channels. "
"The root ``phy`` channel controls the system clock and full-scale output "
"current. Sub-channels provide independent control over single tone profiles, "
"parallel port modulation, digital ramp generation (DRG), RAM playback and "
"output shift keying (OSK)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:21
msgid "Channel hierarchy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:23
msgid ""
"The driver exposes the following IIO output channels, each identified by a "
"unique channel number and a human-readable label. The ``phy`` channel is the "
"root of the hierarchy. Changing its ``sampling_frequency`` reconfigures the "
"system clock (SYSCLK) which affects all other channels."
msgstr ""

