#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:312
msgid "Parallel Port mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:314
msgid ""
"The parallel port allows real-time modulation of DDS parameters through a 16-"
"bit external data bus. The driver exposes separate typed channels for each "
"modulation target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:319
msgid "Non-polar modulation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:321
msgid ""
"In non-polar mode each DDS parameter is controlled by an independent 16-bit "
"bus input. The parallel port channels expose the resolution and base offset "
"of their respective bus inputs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:334 ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:340
#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:372 ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:382
#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:455 ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:760
msgid "``scale``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:336
msgid ""
"Phase resolution per parallel bus LSB. Fixed at :math:`\\pi / 2^{15}` rad/"
"LSB (full 16-bit POW resolution)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:342
msgid ""
"Outputs the frequency scale evaluated as :math:`f_{SYSCLK} \\cdot FM / 2^{32}"
"`. Assuming that :math:`f_{SYSCLK}` is fixed, it is used to configure the "
"modulation gain :math:`FM`, which is a power-of-2 multiplier in "
"range :math:`[1, 32768]`. Writing to this attribute rounds up to the "
"nearest :math:`FM` power of 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:349 ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:377
#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:387
msgid "``offset``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:351
msgid ""
"Outputs the frequency offset in raw units evaluated as :math:`FTW / FM`. "
"Assuming that :math:`FM` is fixed, it is used to configure the FTW register, "
"which is a 32-bit unsigned integer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:356
msgid "Polar modulation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:358
msgid ""
"In polar mode a single 16-bit bus word carries both amplitude (high byte) "
"and phase (low byte). The ``parallel_polar_amplitude`` and "
"``parallel_polar_phase`` channels configure the bias applied to the low-"
"order bits of the ASF and POW registers respectively:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:373 ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:761
msgid "mA/LSB"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:374
msgid ""
"Full-scale amplitude resolution (read-only, fixed at :math:`I_{FS} / 2^{8}`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:378 ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:388
msgid "fractional (raw units)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:379
msgid "Amplitude bias. Lower 6 bits of ASF register. Range :math:`[0, 1)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:383
msgid "rad/LSB"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:384
msgid "Phase resolution (read-only, fixed at :math:`\\pi / 2^{7}`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:389
msgid "Phase bias. Lower 8 bits of POW register. Range :math:`[0, 1)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:394
msgid ""
"Set parallel port frequency modulation with a modulation gain of 16 and a 50 "
"MHz offset:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:405
msgid ""
"One should choose a frequency scale that allows all the desired frequencies "
"to be represented in the 16-bit bus range, i.e., :math:`scale = (f_{max} - "
"f_{min}) / 2^{16}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:411
msgid "Digital ramp generator (DRG)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:413
msgid ""
"The DRG produces linear frequency, phase or amplitude sweeps using dedicated "
"hardware. The active ramp target (destination) is selected by enabling the "
"corresponding typed channel at channel number 130:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:417
msgid "``out_frequency130`` (label ``drg_frequency``) — ramp targets frequency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:418
msgid "``out_phase130`` (label ``drg_phase``) — ramp targets phase"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:419
msgid ""
"``out_altcurrent130`` (label ``drg_amplitude``) — ramp targets amplitude"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:421
msgid ""
"Writing ``en=1`` to one of these channels enables the DRG and switches its "
"destination. Writing ``en=0`` disables the DRG if the channel is the current "
"active destination; writing to an already-inactive destination is a no-op."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:425
msgid ""
"Each destination channel also exposes a read-only ``scale`` attribute "
"reporting the physical quantity per ramp register LSB, which allows "
"converting raw limit codes to physical values."
msgstr ""

