msgid ""
"Read-only. Physical quantity per raw units. Multiply a ramp rising/falling "
"channel ``raw`` value by this scale to get the physical ramp target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:462
msgid "Ramp channel attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:471
msgid "``dwell_en``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:473
msgid ""
"Enable dwell at the ramp limit. When disabled, the ramp auto-transitions at "
"this limit without waiting for the DRCTL pin. Disabling both creates a "
"bidirectional continuous ramp (triangular pattern). Other combinations "
"create single-shot ramps at the DRCTL pin transition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:480
msgid "integer (64-bit)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:481
msgid ""
"Ramp limit expressed as a raw DRG register code in :math:`[0, 2^{32}-1]`. "
"The physical value is ``raw * scale`` where ``scale`` is read from the "
"active destination channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:485 ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:560
#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:705 ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:753
msgid "``sampling_frequency``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:487
msgid ""
"Ramp clock rate. Controlled by an integer divider; the written value is "
"adjusted to the nearest supported rate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:490 ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:692
msgid "``raw_roc``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:491 ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:693
#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:700
msgid "/s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:492
msgid ""
"Rate of change. Number of register codes advanced per second, computed from "
"the hardware step size and the current ramp clock. Writing requires "
"``sampling_frequency`` to be configured first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:499
msgid ""
"Configure a frequency sweep from 40 MHz to 60 MHz with a rate of change of "
"25 GHz/s:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:529
msgid "RAM mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:531
msgid ""
"The AD9910 contains a 1024 x 32-bit RAM that can be loaded with waveform "
"data and played back to modulate frequency, phase, amplitude, or polar "
"(phase + amplitude) parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:536
msgid "RAM control channel attributes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:547
msgid ""
"Enable/disable RAM playback. Toggling swaps profile registers between single "
"tone and RAM configurations across all 8 profiles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:552
msgid ""
"Frequency tuning word used as the single tone frequency when RAM destination "
"is not ``frequency``. Range: :math:`[0, f_{SYSCLK} / 2)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:557
msgid ""
"Phase offset word used as the single tone phase when RAM destination is not "
"``phase``. Range: :math:`[0, 2\\pi)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:562
msgid ""
"RAM playback step rate of the active profile, which controls how fast the "
"address counter advances. Controlled by an integer divider; the written "
"value is adjusted to the nearest supported rate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:567
msgid "Loading RAM data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../iio/ad9910.rst:569
msgid ""
"RAM data is loaded through the firmware upload framework. The driver "
"registers a firmware upload sysfs entry named ``iio_deviceX:ram``. The "
"firmware data follows a binary format (version 1) with an 80-byte header "
"followed by data words. All fields are big-endian."
